node_modules/
**/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
*.lcov
.turbo/
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Agent scratch: SDD ledger, briefs, reports, review packages
.superpowers/

# Planning documents. They were tracked while the kernel was being built from a
# committed spec; CLAUDE.md is the authoritative one now and the plans it
# outlived live in git history. Ignored so they cannot grow back.
docs/superpowers/

# The emitted Prisma contract, minted by the persistence example's `generate`
# script (run by its `test` / `typecheck` scripts). Prisma 8 emits the runtime
# IR and the types beside the contract source rather than into a generated
# client directory; the source itself, `contract.prisma`, is committed.
# Ignored at the root so a checkout predating the package cannot leave one
# visible and sweepable into a commit.
**/src/prisma/contract.json
**/src/prisma/contract.d.ts
**/src/generated/prisma/

# The shared test infrastructure's cross-process locks — `internal/test-infra`
# holds one while it starts or reuses a container, so turbo running several
# workspaces at once cannot start the same container twice. Repository-local
# rather than in the OS temp directory so a stale one is findable.
.cache/

# The docs site's build outputs. TypeDoc runs from `docs/` and writes straight
# into `docs/api/<name>/`, and the hub `docs/api/index.md` with them — it named
# three pre-rename packages for a year because it was the one list nothing
# generated or checked (issue #191).
docs/.vitepress/cache/
docs/.vitepress/dist/
docs/api/*/
docs/api/index.md

# A leftover from Prisma's SQLite era: `prisma migrate` writes a shadow
# database next to the schema, and this example's was committed by accident.
# The suites run against the shared PostgreSQL container, so nothing reads it.
examples/order-infrastructure/.migrate.db
**/src/generated/doc-samples/

# `.claude/` is local agent state — worktrees, transcripts, per-machine
# settings. `skills/` is the exception: a skill is spec that `CLAUDE.md` points
# at, so it has to travel with the repo or the pointer resolves to nothing on
# every machine but this one. It also puts the skill back on the markdown gate,
# which reads this file since `gitignore: true`. This has to be `.claude/*`
# rather than `.claude/`: git cannot re-include a path inside an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so the negation below would never fire.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
